# Plan (opus, strong)

## Goal

Every card-layout picker (`isCardLayout(picker)`: discover, hand, pick, mulligan, and a card-layout embiggen price or short X) gets a `prompt-peek` toggle. Pressing it folds the picker into a slim bar holding the title and a "Back to the choice" button. It also sets `data-collapsed` on `prompt-modal` and `prompt-scrim`, clears the dim and takes the options out of the DOM. Pressing it again brings the picker back with the same selection, so Confirm sends exactly what it would have sent without the fold. Folding sends nothing, a new `choiceId` opens unfolded, and the board pickers (target, zone, tribute, direction, mode, number, cell, the stepper X) are not changed. The work is covered by vitest and by a Cypress component spec at 390×844, with an i18n entry and doc item B47.

## Files to touch

| File | new/change | What |
|---|---|---|
| `apps/web/src/game/Prompt.tsx` | change | header comment; `PromptModal`: `folded` state, `data-collapsed`, `aria-modal`, folded rendering, the `prompt-peek` button |
| `apps/web/src/game/prompt.css` | change | new section: folded scrim and the folded bar |
| `apps/web/src/i18n/zh-CN.json` | change | entry `"Back to the choice"` |
| `apps/web/src/game/Prompt.test.tsx` | change | new `describe` with 5 tests |
| `e2e/cypress/component/mobile-ux.cy.tsx` | change | header line; `CLEAR`, `backgroundOf`; B47 `describe` |
| `docs/polish/7-mobile-ux.md` | change | S6 row, B47 item, Tests row |

Do not touch: anything in `crates/`, `spec/`, `BUILD.md`, `apps/web/src/wire/`, `Game.tsx`, `MarketPrompt.tsx`, `craft/`, `drag/`, or `.github/`, `.harness/`, `.squishy/`, `bot/`. SPEC §10.6 and §10.10 are only read. The change is presentation only (CLAUDE.md rule 7), so it needs no ruling and no wire change.

## Steps

1. **`Prompt.tsx`, header comment.** After the paragraph that ends "…because their answers already glow on the board." (line 38), add:
   ```
   //
   // #1204: a card picker (`isCardLayout`) has "View the board" (`prompt-peek`), which folds it to a bar
   // of its title and "Back to the choice" over an undimmed board (`data-collapsed` on the panel and the
   // scrim, prompt.css). Presentation only: the picks so far stay in `PromptModal`'s state, the fold
   // sends nothing, and a new prompt is a new `PromptModal` (its `key`), so it opens unfolded.
   ```

2. **`Prompt.tsx`, `PromptModal`.** Directly after `const panel = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);` (line 1004), add:
   ```tsx
   /** #1204: the card picker folded to a bar so the board shows. Never sent; `selected` outlasts it. */
   const [folded, setFolded] = useState(false);
   ```

3. **`Prompt.tsx`, `PromptModal`'s returned JSX** (lines 1263–1317). Keep every existing slot where it is: each conditional stays its own JSX child, so React keeps the peek button's DOM node (and its focus) across the toggle.
   - a. On the `prompt-scrim` div add `data-collapsed={folded ? "true" : undefined}`.
   - b. On the `prompt-modal` div add `data-collapsed={folded ? "true" : undefined}` after `data-board-testids`, and replace `aria-modal="true"` with `aria-modal={!folded}`.
   - c. Wrap everything from `<p className="prompt-count">` through `{props.source === "play" ? <BoardHint chrome={picker.chrome} /> : null}` in `{folded ? null : (<> … </>)}`. That covers count, `props.status`, `body()`, the board note, the comment and `BoardHint`. The reward banner and `<PickerTitle …/>` stay outside the wrapper.
   - d. Inside `.prompt-actions`, wrap the `prompt-submit` button in `{folded ? null : ( … )}`. Change the cancel condition to `{folded || props.onCancel === undefined ? null : ( … )}`. After it, as the last child, add:
     ```tsx
     {isCardLayout(picker) ? (
       <button type="button" data-testid="prompt-peek" aria-pressed={folded} onClick={() => setFolded((was) => !was)}>
         {folded ? t("Back to the choice") : t("View the board")}
       </button>
     ) : null}
     ```
     Leave `Prompt`, `pickerForPending`, `pickerForNeed` and the keys (`pending.choiceId`, `needKey(need)`) unchanged. Those keys are what reset the fold for a new prompt.

4. **`prompt.css`.** Insert this section right after the closing `}` of `@media (orientation: landscape) and (max-height: 500px) { … }` (line 935) and before the comment `/* R514: while a cell prompt is open …`. It must come after that block: its `.prompt[data-prompt-kind] .prompt-actions button` has the same specificity. Do **not** open a new `@media (max-width: 600px) {` block anywhere, because `board-ux.test.tsx` B44 slices the file from that string's last occurrence.
   ```css
   /* --- a card picker folded to show the board (#1204, docs/polish/7-mobile-ux.md B47) --------- */

   /* "View the board" (Prompt.tsx `prompt-peek`) folds a card picker to a slim bar on the bottom edge,
      its title and "Back to the choice" as B44's bar lays them out, over a scrim with no dim, so the
      whole board can be read before choosing. The scrim stays click-through, so hover, tap-to-inspect
      and the clock work as under any picker. The small pickers never fold and keep their dock. */
   .prompt-scrim[data-collapsed] {
     place-items: end center;
     background: transparent;
   }

   .prompt[data-collapsed] {
     display: grid;
     grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
     grid-template-areas: "title actions";
     align-items: center;
     gap: 0 8px;
     padding-top: 6px;
     padding-bottom: max(6px, env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
   }

   .prompt[data-collapsed] > .prompt-title {
     grid-area: title;
     min-width: 0;
     overflow: hidden;
     text-overflow: ellipsis;
     white-space: nowrap;
   }

   /* No list scrolls under the button, so the sticky footer's rule and gap would only make the bar taller. */
   .prompt[data-collapsed] > .prompt-actions {
     grid-area: actions;
     margin: 0;
     padding-top: 0;
     border-top: 0;
   }

   .prompt[data-collapsed] > .prompt-actions button {
     flex: 0 0 auto;
     padding-inline: 12px;
   }
   ```
   The phone block's `.prompt button { min-height: 44px }` already gives the toggle its 44 px.

5. **`zh-CN.json`.** After the line `"Highlighted on the board as well.": "棋盘上也已高亮显示。",` add `"Back to the choice": "返回选择",`. `"View the board"` already has an entry (line 29).

